{{/*
Model pin for the crush-signal harness — MANAGED, not create_.

This file used to be create_private_crush.json.tmpl, seed-once-then-never-touch,
and that is exactly how it broke. Crush's TUI model picker rewrites its config
in place, so a model switched during a live Signal session is written to the
TARGET — and because create_ means "write only if absent", chezmoi had no
opinion about it ever again. The pin below said zai/glm-5.2 while the running
agent had drifted to hyper/kimi-k3: $3.27/M in and $16.33/M out, the priciest
model in Hyper's catalog, at max reasoning effort, on an always-on agent
against a metered account with auto-top-up behind it. `harness list` still
described it as "GLM-5.2 (Z.ai)" the whole time.

Managed means the drift cannot recur: an apply now reverts the target. The
trade is deliberate and it is the entire point — a model chosen in the TUI
lasts until the next czu, and a permanent change is an edit HERE.

Same trap harness.toml was pulled out of; see its header for the other half.

PROVIDER CHOICE. Both slots go through LiteLLM. large names the BALANCED
group glm-5.3-balanced — one model name over a Z.ai deployment and a Hyper
one — so the router fails over per request and neither provider's quota can
strand this agent. small runs ai01's local Qwen, which is free and has no
quota at all.

@joestump-agent 09/14/2026 - This used to read "Z.ai is quota-metered, not
pay-per-token, so a busy week degrades to a hard stop rather than to a bill.
That is the property this always-on agent wants. Hyper stays the metered
overflow and nothing here should point at it." On 09/14 the hard stop arrived
and it was not the property we wanted: Z.ai's weekly cap emptied, every
always-on worker on tars and kitt died together, and the Switchboard forge
queue went ~20h undrained with the reset four days out. Balanced, a wall costs
a retry instead of an outage.

  large  glm-5.3-balanced  Signal work, failing over across Z.ai and Hyper
  small  Qwen3.8-27B    titles and summaries, which fire on every exchange —
                        the cheapest way to keep those off the large quota.
                        Replaces glm-4.7-flashx, two generations stale.

@joestump-agent 08/28/2026 - Converted from create_ to managed after the pin
  drifted to hyper/kimi-k3 undetected, and repointed small at glm-5.3-flash.

@joestump-agent 08/30/2026 - large glm-5.2 -> glm-5.3-flash, per Joe. Both
  tiers are now the same model, which is the point: flash is a generation
  newer than 5.2 and cheaper against the same quota, and the note above
  claiming "the 5.3 tier buys nothing here" was written before 5.3-flash
  existed as an option for the large slot.

  `harness list` also described these as "GLM-5.2 (Z.ai)" while the harness
  itself carried no model pin at all -- the model has always come from THIS
  file via CRUSH_GLOBAL_DATA. The description strings are corrected in
  harness.toml.tmpl so the listing stops asserting a pin that does not live
  there.
*/ -}}
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "models": {
    "large": { "model": "glm-5.3-balanced", "provider": "litellm" },
    "small": { "model": "Qwen3.8-27B", "provider": "litellm" }
  }
}
